# Lure on a creature with menace (CR 509.1c, its example): the declaration must obey as many requirements as one that breaks
# no restriction can. Bot1's Callous Inspector (1/1 menace) wears Lure and attacks; Bot2 has two creatures able to block it.
# One blocking alone breaks menace's restriction (CR 702.110b), no block obeys none of the two requirements, and both
# blocking obeys both - the only legal declaration. The Inspector dies, dealing its 1 to Bot2's Elves first, and its "when
# this creature dies, it deals 1 damage to you" hits Bot1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Callous Inspector
Black Lotus
Lure
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Ornithopter
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Callous Inspector.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Lure.Cast(Callous Inspector)
Bot1.Attack(Callous Inspector > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Count: 0)
! Bot2.Block(Llanowar Elves > Callous Inspector)
Bot2.Block(Llanowar Elves > Callous Inspector; Ornithopter > Callous Inspector)
Bot1.AssignDamage(Callous Inspector > Llanowar Elves: 1)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Life = 19
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Lure; Callous Inspector; Black Lotus
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
